    description: "Dart's signature renderer cuts a default value at its first comma, and named parameters hash \"name =\".\n\nREPRO: void f({Size s = const Size(1, 2)}) renders the signature ({Size s = ..., 2)}). Cause: _extract_dart_signature's re.sub(r'\\s*=\\s*[^,}\\]]+', ...) stops at the first comma inside the default. Named parameters also keep \"name =\" in the hashed text. Found during WI-tojov (PR 3, commit 4e0163454): the item attributed Dart fragments to split_params_top_level, but they come from this regex. Evidence: /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/pr3/tojov/RESULTS.md residual 2. Changing it moves Dart typed ids, so it needs a scheme bump."  # ec5f
